```javascript
const status = document.querySelector('[data-status]');
const message = '<strong>Saved</strong>';

status.textContent = message;
status.classList.toggle('is-success', true);
```
The angle brackets appear as text; they are not parsed into an element.

```javascript
const profile = document.querySelector('[data-profile]');
const nameFromApi = '<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>';

profile.textContent = nameFromApi;
```
The browser creates a text node, not an image element.
